message I’ll identify the harness incident log and confirm how the dashboard totals are calculated before clearing anything. I’ll preserve unrelated project data and report the before/after totals.
read /bin/zsh -lc "rg --files -g '"'!*node_modules*'"' -g '"'!*.lock'"' | sed -n '1,240p'"
read /bin/zsh -lc "ls -la && rg -n -i \"incident|harness|dashboard|total|log\" . --hidden -g '"'!node_modules'"' -g '"'!.git'"'"
message This request maps to the harness’s built-in doctor mode, which owns the incident ledger and dashboard summary. I’m using the `msg` skill so the cleanup follows the harness’s own retention and counting
read /bin/zsh -lc "sed -n '1,260p' .agents/skills/msg/SKILL.md"
shell /bin/zsh -lc "wc -l .agents/skills/shared/refs/codex-runtime.md .agents/skills/msg/refs/compatibility-map.md .agents/skills/msg/CLAUDE-SKILL.md && sed -n '1,360p' .agents/skills/shared/refs/codex-runtime.md && sed -n '1,320p' .agents/skills/msg/refs/compatibility-map.md && sed -n '1,420p' .agents/skills/msg/CLAUDE-SKILL.md"
read /bin/zsh -lc "sed -n '1,140p' .agents/skills/msg/refs/compatibility-map.md && sed -n '141,300p' .agents/skills/msg/refs/compatibility-map.md && sed -n '1,320p' .agents/skills/msg/refs/protocol-doctor.md && sed -n '1,240p' .agents/skills/shared/refs/doctor-logging.md && sed -n '1,220p' .agents/skills/shared/refs/closing-message.md"
shell /bin/zsh -lc 'find . -maxdepth 3 -type f -print | sort && find . -maxdepth 3 -type d -print | sort && git status --short --untracked-files=all'
message The repository does not currently contain `devkit/DOCTOR.md`, so there is no incident ledger here to clear or count. I’m running the harness’s tally once to confirm the missing-ledger result rather th
shell /bin/zsh -lc '.agents/scripts/script-doctor-tally.sh devkit/DOCTOR.md'
message 🔴 Fail! No incident ledger exists at `devkit/DOCTOR.md`, so nothing was cleared and totals cannot be calculated. | What happened | Detail | |---|---| | Cleanup | No changes made | | Totals | Unavailab
